title ALES74 — Lotus's tremolo, the triangle LFO turned on amplitude
prompt recur the itinerary Lindy-first crux-first, take the next agent-doable lap, approve own design rounds, send each finished increment, stop at custody gates
think ALES71–73 all point the triangle LFO at ONE target — the delay: the chorus mixes the swinging copy, the vibrato hears it alone, the flanger feeds it back. The LFO driver triangle_delay_at is a GENERAL scaled triangle, though — named for its first use, it knows nothing of delay. Lindy-first, the family had not yet grown modulation of AMPLITUDE, the primitive auto-pan and the ring modulator will stand on; crux-first, the decisive recognition is that the SAME triangle that drove the delay drives the gain — a new target, no new arithmetic.
think The thinning is the reward. Every earlier delay rung snapshotted the dry prefix BECAUSE a moving read must not read a sample it just wrote. The tremolo's output depends only on its OWN input sample — never a neighbour — so it writes IN PLACE WITH NO SNAPSHOT; the whole frozen-prefix machinery falls away. This is the thinnest rung in the modulation family, and the honest reason is stated as an invariant, not assumed.
think Held the gain to an ATTENUATION — 0 ≤ g ≤ glide_scale (floor at silence via BadDepth centre − depth < 0, top at unity via BadGain centre + depth > glide_scale). So x·g/scale is never louder than x and already fits the i16 rail: the write's saturate is a proven no-op, exactly as the vibrato's wet-only write never clips. A gain above unity would risk the rail and is refused rather than silently saturated.
think Chose centre scale/2, depth scale/2, period 4 for the hand-computed law — the four quarter anchors trace ½ → 1 → ½ → 0, so a steady 1000 becomes 500,1000,500,0,500,1000, each an exact integer. Proved the family recognition directly: a DC signal traces triangle_delay_at sample-by-sample. Zero-depth is a constant-gain fader; unity+zero-depth passes sample_min through byte-for-byte (the saturate no-op made visible at the very edge of the rail).
obs GREEN on the first build across all six laws — no RED. Faults: BadPeriod (odd/zero/wide), BadDepth (negative depth or floor below silence), BadGain (top past unity), BadRange — each refusing before any write, the clip untouched; there is NO BadDelay and NO BadLevel (no delay line, the gain IS the level). tame_style_check bans clean, ratchets printed. The design read was self-approved (no custody gate — bounded in-process i16 PCM, no network/keys/funds/device/sample-rate).
loom witness=ales_tremolo_witness laws=6 green=1 reuses=triangle_delay_at glide_scale=256 period_law=multiple_of_4 gain=attenuation snapshot=none
file lotus/tremolo.rye ALES74 — the triangle LFO read as a gain, y[i]=saturate(x[i]·g(i)/glide_scale), in place with no snapshot; reuses ALES71's driver
file tools/ales_tremolo_witness.rish witness GREEN, proves a steady signal traces the triangle gain and each fault refuses by name
file active-designing/20260814-201204_fill-ales74-lotus-tremolo-amplitude-modulation.md design read for the rung, self-approved round
file lotus/README.md Status rung list + stamp carry ALES74
recommend keep-going ALES75 — auto-pan (the same LFO on ALES10's stereo field, a voice swung left-right rather than up-down in loudness) or the ring modulator (a faster carrier on the same gain); both stand on this proven amplitude-LFO path
